  "configuration_notes": [
    "Application and framework source remain unmodified. Local fixture helpers under app/tmp bootstrap the checked-out models; they are not part of the book or upstream application changes.",
    "The capture fixture temporarily enables MISP.background_jobs, Plugin.Workflow_enable and new audit logging, using separate job Redis DB 13 and loopback-only Supervisor XML-RPC. All automatic core triggers remain disabled, no recurring task is saved, and no event is published or synchronized.",
    "Six real Supervisor-managed workers run as the fixture OS user. One job executes Admin redisReady, completes through the default worker and is displayed in Jobs. Worker status, showQueues and showJobStatus are checked. No publication, ingestion or email job is queued.",
    "A temporary local organisation-admin account verifies own-organisation user listing, rejection of another organisation user and site/workflow settings, disabled-account API rejection and re-enabled access. Credentials are never captured; the account and its keys are removed after the checks.",
    "The core demonstration graph is Event Before Save -> IF Generic -> Stop execution. Only graph validation and side-effect-free condition/stop module tests execute against synthetic inputs. Disabled full-workflow invocation is verified as success with Module disabled, not claimed as end-to-end blocking enforcement.",
    "A separate manual workflow is created but remains disabled and is never invoked. Thirteen default blueprint definitions are loaded from the pinned local submodule; importing definitions does not activate workflows.",
    "Admin migrationStatus --json and schemaDiagnostics show an up-to-date local ledger: 131 applied migrations, no failed/deferred/pending entries. migrationApply --dry-run is verified only on that up-to-date state, where there is no SQL to render. No upgrade, conversion or restore is performed by these checks.",
    "Admin valueDictionaryStats refreshes local statistics for the values index. It is a cache/statistics write, not a read-only report; the guide makes that distinction.",
    "The local database connection encoding is aligned with the current diagnostic recommendation. This is ignored fixture configuration, not a schema migration or a production change.",
    "Mail, OTP mandate, AI, Kafka and ZeroMQ publishing remain disabled. No credentials are emailed, OTP enrollment/reset performed, external module/provider called, connector upload attempted, backup restored or 2.5-to-3.0 migration rehearsed.",
    "The PHP capture process retains the session proxy and CA trust; only loopback/local Docker names bypass the proxy. The application is reached over Docker-local/loopback HTTP for capture. Documentation requires the actual deployment HTTPS and trust configuration.",
    "Remote version-check failures and optional-service findings are shown as observed, not retouched into a healthy production deployment. The workflow editor retains its own canvas layout in this application branch.",
    "After capture/checks, both disabled example workflows and the temporary org-admin account/keys were deleted. Supervisor was shut down and the original local config.php/database.php restored. Blueprint files/definitions remain in the local training fixture."
  ],
